            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for pitifulness, then the Tamil for concern."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: கதறு",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கதறு — kataṟu — \"to wail; to cry out\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அந்தச் செய்தியைக் கேட்டு அவள் கதறி அழுதாள். antac ceytiyaik kēṭṭu avaḷ kataṟi aḻutāḷ. Hearing the news, she wailed and wept."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): கதறினேன், kataṟiṉēṉ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Often கதறி அழு, to cry aloud."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கதறு (kataṟu) is native Dravidian (DEDR 1189); Malayalam has the same verb for roaring."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
